[/LIST]

[CENTER][SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8a51c4]🚀 Why It's Efficient[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]1. Chunk-Based System[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]Aligned with Minecraft's architecture for maximum performance. Chunks are the natural unit of entity management.[/COLOR]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]2. Multi-Level Caching[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]Using Caffeine cache with configurable TTL reduces redundant calculations and database queries.[/COLOR]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]3. Async-First Threading[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]All heavy operations run asynchronously using ForkJoinPool and custom thread pools. Main thread only touches Bukkit API.[/COLOR]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]4. Object Pooling[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]ChunkKey pooling reduces garbage collection pressure and memory allocations.[/COLOR]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]5. Fast-Path Optimization[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]Immediate returns for entity types without limits avoid unnecessary processing.[/COLOR]

[B][COLOR=#8fffc1]6. Batch Processing[/COLOR][/B]
[COLOR=#e7cfff]Entities are grouped by chunk before removal, reducing scheduler overhead.[/COLOR]

